title: NOT from a NAND
mode: draw
chapter: NAND does everything
check: behaves
parts: nand
---- intro
Remember the fun fact from the NAND lesson: with enough NAND gates you can build **any** circuit. This chapter shows it. The parts list has only NAND gates.

Look at the NAND table again, at the two rows where both inputs are the same:

| a | b | NAND |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | 0 | 1 |
| 1 | 1 | 0 |

If both inputs get the same wire, NAND gives the opposite of it.
---- task
Build a NOT gate out of one NAND gate: `y` is the opposite of `a`.
---- start
input a 0 20
led y 300 20
---- reference
input a
led y
y = ~a
---- answer
input a 0 20
nand g1 140 20
led y 300 20
a -> g1.0
a -> g1.1
g1 -> y
---- hint1
Both of the NAND gate's inputs can come from the same switch: drag from `a` twice.
---- hint2
`a` into both inputs of the NAND gate, and its output into `y`.
---- solution
`a` goes into both inputs of the NAND. 0 NAND 0 is 1, and 1 NAND 1 is 0: a NOT gate.
---- done
One NAND, wired to itself, is a NOT. Next: AND.
